<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Bridges are critical arteries of our transportation networks, facilitating economic activity and connecting communities. However, they face relentless challenges from dynamic loads, environmental stressors, and the inevitable march of time. Aging infrastructure, coupled with the constant assault of traffic and weather, leads to cracks, fatigue, and structural degradation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Traditional manual inspections, while diligent, suffer from inherent limitations: they are often infrequent, subjective, and prone to human error. This approach can miss nascent issues, allowing minor problems to escalate into critical failures.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
